Vary one interior point $x_n$, holding every other $x_k$ fixed. Only two terms in the sum depend on $x_n$: $\begin{aligned}
  A_\epsilon\big|_{x_n}
  &=
  \epsilon L\left(x_n,\frac{x_{n+1}-x_n}{\epsilon}\right)
  \notag\\
  &\quad+
  \epsilon L\left(x_{n-1},
                  \frac{x_n-x_{n-1}}{\epsilon}\right).
  \end{aligned}$ Differentiating gives $\begin{aligned}
  0=\frac{\partial A_\epsilon}{\partial x_n}
  &=
  \epsilon\frac{\partial L_n}{\partial x_n}
  -\frac{\partial L_n}{\partial v_n}
  +\frac{\partial L_{n-1}}{\partial v_{n-1}}.
  \end{aligned}$ The opposite signs have a simple geometric origin. Raising $x_n$ increases the slope of the interval behind it and decreases the slope of the interval ahead of it.

